dialect protocol
protocol stdio.bcf.diff
version 1
schema stdio.bcf
start record

# FG-wave: REAL binary diff frame, replacing F6's `print_diff().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`../../🦀️component.rs`'s old `DiffCodec::encode_diff`/`decode_diff`) -- per this
# ticket's own `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §4/§6 census, 100% of stdio's `DiffCodec` impls were still on
# this shortcut before this pilot ladder. `format u8` + `flags u8` (bit0 = `version` present, bit1
# = `topics` present, bit2 = `parts` present -- `BcfDiff`'s exact THREE independently-optional
# top-level fields, in that field-declaration order) as two REAL fixed fields, individually
# protocol-walked -- same shape `📜️docx/…/🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️component.protocol.semio`'s own
# `flags` header uses (restated here, per-artifact bit assignment; bcf needs 3 bits where docx's
# `DocxDiff` only needed 2, since bcf's own `BcfDiff` has one more top-level field).
#
# Past that header, `version`/`topics`/`parts` (whichever `flags` marks present, in that FIXED
# order) are bundled into ONE opaque trailing `bytes` chain: `topics`'s own recursive
# `NamedTripleDiff<String,BcfTopicDiff,BcfTopic>` nests BACK through a modified topic's own
# `comments`/`viewpoints` collection triples, and `viewpoints`' own `BcfViewpointDiff.camera` field
# reaches the genuinely data-carrying `BcfCamera` enum -- the SAME `protocol-prim-ref-recursion`
# mechanism gap every other stdio artifact's diff payload hits (`Prim::Ref` unconditionally errors
# in `walk_protocol`, confirmed unchanged through every pilot, `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §5). This
# dialect's `Cond` also cannot test an individual FLAG BIT (only a field's whole value against a
# literal), so a per-bit-guarded field list isn't expressible even before the recursion is
# considered -- `version` itself IS flat/non-recursive, but bundling it into the same opaque tail
# as `topics`/`parts` (rather than describing it alone as a real field) keeps ONE single decode
# path honest and simple, the same minimal-surface choice docx's own diff protocol file documents.
#
# The Rust `encode_diff`/`decode_diff` side stays genuinely, fully structured past this header --
# real LEB128-varint-framed collection counts, per-field 1-byte tri-state presence tags, and
# recursive per-variant binary sub-encoders for `BcfTopic`/`BcfTopicDiff`/`BcfComment`/
# `BcfCommentDiff`/`BcfViewpoint`/`BcfViewpointDiff`/`BcfCamera`/`BcfComponents`/`BcfRawPart`/
# `BcfPartDiff` (see `../../🦀️component.rs`'s own `BinaryPrimitives`/`ValueBinaryCodecs`/
# `GenericNamedTripleBinaryCodecs`/`DiffValueBinaryCodecs` regions) -- round-trip tested
# independently of this protocol description, same honest-boundary treatment
# `📖️grammar-recipe.md` §2.5 documents.
framing record
header fixed 2
field format u8
field flags u8
chain payload bytes
